To find the first point that falls outside the square on a line drawn from the given point in the given direction, you can use the following steps:

1. Calculate the distance from the given point to the square's edge in the given direction.
2. Check if the distance is greater than half the side length of the square.
3. If the distance is greater than half the side length, return that point as the first point that falls outside the square.
4. If the distance is not greater than half the side length, repeat the process with the line extended in the opposite direction until the distance is greater than half the side length.

Here is some sample code to implement this algorithm in Unity C#:
```scss
public Vector2 FindEdgePoint(Vector2 point, Vector2 direction, float sideLength) {
    // Calculate the distance from the point to the square's edge in the given direction
    float distance = Vector2.Dot(direction, new Vector2(sideLength, 0)) / Vector2.Dot(new Vector2(1, 1), direction);

    // Check if the distance is greater than half the side length of the square
    if (distance > sideLength / 2) {
        return point + direction * distance;
    }

    // If the distance is not greater than half the side length, repeat the process with the line extended in the opposite direction
    return FindEdgePoint(point + direction * distance, -direction, sideLength);
}
```
You can call this function with the given point, direction, and side length of the square as arguments:
```java
Vector2 point = new Vector2(0.25f, 0.25f);
Vector2 direction = new Vector2(1, 0);
float sideLength = 0.5f;

Vector2 edgePoint = FindEdgePoint(point, direction, sideLength);
```
This will return the first point that falls outside the square on a line drawn from the given point in the given direction.

