```javascript
methods: {
    resetAndRedraw() {
        // Remove the old graph
        d3.select("#graph").selectAll("*").remove();

        // Get your new data (replace this with your actual data fetching logic)
        let newData = this.getNewData();

        // Draw the new graph
        this.drawGraph(newData);
    }
}
```

Please note that `#graph` is assumed to be the id of the SVG or div containing the graph. Replace it with the actual id of your SVG or div.

When you want to reset and redraw your graph, you can simply call `this.resetAndRedraw()` in your Vue.js component. Remember, the D3 select method is used to select the SVG container and the selectAll("*").remove() is used to remove all the child elements, effectively clearing the SVG container.

Also, you should replace `this.getNewData()` with your actual logic for fetching the new data you want to render. After clearing the SVG container and fetching the new data, you can then call `this.drawGraph(newData)` to draw the new bar graph with the new data.

