Here's a basic Python script that recursively scans a directory and returns True if any files have been modified since the previous time the script was run, and False if no changes have been made:

```py
import os

def check_dir(dir):
    if not os.path.exists(dir):
        return False

    for file in os.listdir(dir):
        if file.endswith(".py") or file.endswith(".txt") or file.endswith(".conf"):
            check_dir(os.path.join(dir, file))

    return os.path.exists(os.path.join(dir, "last_modified"))

if __name__ == "__main__":
    dir = "/path/to/directory"
    if check_dir(dir):
        print("Files have been modified since the previous time the script was run.")
    else:
