Here's a sample Siemens S7 code that uses the analog input channel ADC to read in data samples at a fixed sampling rate of 100ms per element for an array of 1000 elements:


```scss
Inputs:
  ADC_Channel(10),
  SamplingRate(100),
  NumberOfElements(1000),
  SamplePoint(1000);

DataType: Array[1001, 10];

Function:
  SampleData(ADC_Channel, SamplingRate, NumberOfElements, SamplePoint);

SampleData:
  StartTimer(SamplingRate);
  Do:
    ReadData(ADC_Channel);
    If(TimedOut, StopTimer);
    Array[SamplePoint] = ReadData;
    SamplePoint++;
    If(SamplePoint >= NumberOfElements, StopTimer);
  EndDo;

ReadData:
  ADC_Channel.Read(ReadData);

StopTimer:
  StopTimer();

EndSampleData;

```

In this code, the `` ReadData `` function is used to read data from the analog input channel using the `` Read() `` method. The `` SampleData `` function uses a `` StartTimer() `` and `` Do `` loop structure to read in data at a fixed rate of 100ms per element for the specified number of elements. The `` Array `` data type is used to store the data, and the `` SamplePoint `` variable is used to keep track of the current sample point. The `` TimedOut `` variable is used to detect when the timer has run out, and the `` StopTimer() `` function is called to stop the timer.

