```
public static string IntToStr(int num)
{
    char[] str = new char[10];
    int i = 0;
    while (num > 0)
    {
        str[i] = (char)((num % 10) + '0');
        num /= 10;
        i++;
    }
    Array.Reverse(str);
    return new string(str);
}
```
This function creates an array of characters with a length of 10, and then uses a while loop to iterate through the digits of the number, adding each digit to the beginning of the character array. After the loop, the function calls the `Array.Reverse()` method to reverse the order of the characters in the array, and then returns a new string created from the array.

