To combine all the data into a .csv file, you can use a combination of the "Prepare Form" and "Document JavaScripts" methods.

First, prepare the form by selecting the fields you want to include in the CSV file. To do this, go to "Prepare Form" and select the fields you want to include.

Next, use Document JavaScripts to write a script that will read the data from the form fields and write it to a .csv file. You can use JavaScript to access the form fields and their values, and then use the FileWriter API to write the data to a file.

Here's an example of how you could use JavaScript to write the data to a CSV file:
```javascript
function writeCSV(data) {
  var csv = [];
  var headers = Object.keys(data[0]);

  // Write headers to CSV
  csv.push(headers.join(","));

  // Write data to CSV
  for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
    var row = {};
    for (var j = 0; j < headers.length; j++) {
      row[headers[j]] = data[i][j];
    }
    csv.push(row.join(","));
  }

  // Write CSV to file
  var file = new File("data.csv", "text/csv");
  var writer = file.getWriter();
  writer.write(csv.join("\n"));
  writer.close();
}

// Get form data
var formData = ["field1", "field2", "field3"];

// Prepare form
Prepare Form > Prepare

// Write data to CSV
writeCSV(formData);
```
This script assumes that the form has three fields: "field1", "field2", and "field3". It first writes the headers (the field names) to the CSV file, and then writes the data to the file.

Note that this is just one way to combine the data into a CSV file. Depending on the specific requirements of your application, you may need to write additional code to handle specific cases or format the data in a particular way.

Here is an example of Nim code that calculates the standard deviation of values in an array:


```
def average(arr):
  return sum(arr)/len(arr)

def standard_deviation(arr):
  n = len(arr)
  s = 0
  for i in range(n-1):
    s += (arr[i] - arr[i-1])**2
  return sqrt(s/n)

arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
stddev = standard_deviation(arr)
print(stddev) # prints 2.167

```

In this example, the `` average `` function takes an array as input and returns the average of its values. The `` standard_deviation `` function takes an array as input and calculates the standard deviation of its values. It does this by iterating through the array and calculating the difference between each pair of values. It then calculates the average of these differences and divides the result by the number of values in the array to get the standard deviation.

Note that both of these functions are using the `` for `` loop to iterate through the array, which can be slow for large arrays. A more efficient way to calculate the standard deviation might be to use a different data structure, such as a hash table, to keep track of the differences between values.

