The process of ordering a pizza can be represented by an UML activity diagram to show the steps involved in the activity. Here is an example of how you can model the process using an activity diagram:

1. Start Order: The process begins when the customer decides to order a pizza.
2. Choose Pizza Size: The customer selects the size of the pizza they want to order.
3. Select Toppings: The customer chooses the toppings they want on their pizza.
4. Add to Cart: The selected pizza is added to the shopping cart.
5. Proceed to Checkout: The customer proceeds to the checkout process.
6. Enter Delivery Details: The customer enters the delivery address and other necessary details.
7. Make Payment: The customer makes the payment for the order.
8. Place Order: The order is placed and confirmed.

Here is the plantUML code for the activity diagram:

```plantuml
@startuml
|Start Order|
:Choose Pizza Size;
:Select Toppings;
:Add to Cart;
|Proceed to Checkout|
:Enter Delivery Details;
:Make Payment;
|Place Order|
@enduml
```

You can copy and paste this code into a PlantUML editor to visualize the activity diagram of ordering a pizza.

